<span class="ltx_personname">Pengyu Zhao
</span><span class="ltx_author_notes"><span class="ltx_author_notes_content">
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_affiliation"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Affiliation: </span>MiniMax
</span></span></span></span></div>

<div id="abstract1" class="ltx_abstract"><h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_abstract">Abstract</h6>
    
<p id="abstract1.1" class="ltx_p">Ultra-long-context capability is becoming indispensable for frontier LLMs: agentic workflows, repository-scale code reasoning, and persistent memory all require the model to jointly attend over hundreds of thousands to millions of tokens—yet the quadratic cost of softmax attention makes this untenable at deployment scale. We introduce MiniMax Sparse Attention (<span id="abstract1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MSA</span>), a blockwise sparse attention built upon Grouped Query Attention (GQA).
A lightweight Index Branch scores key–value blocks and independently selects a Top-<math id="abstract1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> subset for each GQA group, enabling group-specific sparse retrieval while maintaining efficient block-level execution; the Main Branch then performs exact block-sparse attention over only the selected blocks. Designed around a principle of simplicity and scalability, <span id="abstract1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MSA</span> is deliberately streamlined, making it straightforward to deploy efficiently across a broad range of GPUs.
To translate sparsity into practical speedups, we co-design <span id="abstract1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MSA</span> with a GPU execution path that uses exp-free Top-<math id="abstract1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> selection and KV-outer sparse attention to improve tensor-core utilization under block-granular access. On a 109B-parameter model with native multimodal training, <span id="abstract1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MSA</span> performs on par with GQA while reducing per-token attention compute by <math id="abstract1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="28.4\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>28.4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">28.4\times</annotation></semantics></math> at 1M context. Paired with our co-designed kernel, <span id="abstract1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MSA</span> achieves <math id="abstract1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="14.2\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>14.2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">14.2\times</annotation></semantics></math> prefill and <math id="abstract1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="7.6\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>7.6</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7.6\times</annotation></semantics></math> decoding wall-clock speedups on H800. Our inference kernel is available at: <a href="https://github.com/MiniMax-AI/MSA" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/MiniMax-AI/MSA</a>. A production-grade natively multimodal model powered by <span id="abstract1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MSA</span> has been publicly released at: <a href="https://huggingface.co/MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-M3" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://huggingface.co/MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-M3</a>.</p>
  
</div>
<figure id="S0.F1" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2606.13392v1/figures/msa_arch.png" id="S0.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/227;" width="476" height="227" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S0.F1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 1</span>: </span><span id="S0.F1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Overview of <span id="S0.F1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MSA</span>. The Index Branch (left) scores the full causal context with a single lightweight head and selects, for each query and GQA group, a set <math id="S0.F1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{I}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{I}}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S0.F1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> key blocks; the local block is always included regardless of its score. The Main Branch (right) attends only to the selected blocks and produces the layer output. During training, a KL loss aligns the index distribution with the group-averaged Main Branch distribution on the selected blocks, and the Index Branch gradient is detached from the Main Branch.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1 </span>Introduction</h2>

<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Large language models (LLMs) are rapidly shifting from short, single-turn interactions to long-horizon agentic workflows that span hundreds of interleaved reasoning and action steps—writing and deploying production code, navigating the open web, orchestrating diverse tools, and producing structured documents <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">OpenAI, 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Anthropic, 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Google DeepMind, 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">DeepSeek-AI, 2026</a>; <a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Moonshot AI, 2026</a>; <a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhipu AI, 2026</a>)</cite>. However, the ultra-long contexts these tasks demand impose severe compute and memory bottlenecks on both training and inference, with quadratic-cost softmax attention being the primary culprit, further amplified by the latency and throughput constraints of production-scale deployment.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Context length is a critical scaling dimension for LLMs, where trading off model quality against efficiency remains a formidable challenge. The community is actively pushing the Pareto frontier on this front. Hybrid architectures <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">MiniMax, 2025b</a>; <a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Qwen, 2026</a>)</cite> replace a subset of softmax attention layers with efficient alternatives such as linear attention <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">Team et al., 2025a</a>; <a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gu and Dao, 2023</a>)</cite> or sliding window attention <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">OpenAI et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">MiMo et al., 2026</a>)</cite>. Alternatively, another line of work attempts to sparsify softmax attention <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">DeepSeek-AI et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">DeepSeek-AI, 2026</a>; <a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">Team et al., 2025b</a>; <a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lu et al., 2025</a>)</cite> itself to break the computational bottleneck.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We introduce MiniMax Sparse Attention (MSA), designed following Occam’s razor: after extensive ablation, we retain only the essential components. MSA follows the sparse softmax attention paradigm to maximally reuse existing software and hardware infrastructure.
We adopt blockwise token selection with a smaller top-<math id="S1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, enabling efficient execution across a wider range of GPU architectures while relaxing the head-dimension constraints imposed by prior designs. Concretely, an ultra-lightweight Index Branch selects, for each attention group, the top-<math id="S1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> blocks via max-pooling scoring, while always retaining the most recent block to ensure training stability.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Turning MSA’s theoretical sparsity into practical end-to-end speedups requires co-designing the algorithm with its GPU execution path. To this end, we design an exp-free TopK kernel specialized for the small-k regime, leveraging the blockwise indexer to bypass unnecessary softmax computation before selection. For the main attention branch, we organize sparse attention in a KV-outer order: selected KV blocks gather their associated queries and concatenate them to fill tensor-core MMAs, using pre-scheduled chunking with a two-phase combine to handle highly skewed block popularity without atomic updates. For training, we further fuse the auxiliary LSE computation required by the sparse KL loss into the forward pass and employ persistent load balancing in the backward pass.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">To validate that MSA preserves both textual and multimodal capabilities, we compare it against Grouped Query Attention on a 109B-parameter Mixture of Experts (MoE) model trained from scratch with a 3T-token budget. MSA matches GQA on downstream benchmarks while delivering <math id="S1.p5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="14.2\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>14.2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">14.2\times</annotation></semantics></math> prefill and <math id="S1.p5.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="7.6\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>7.6</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7.6\times</annotation></semantics></math> decoding speedups at 1M context length.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Main contributions.</span></p>
<ul id="S1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We propose MSA, a minimal, scalable, and accelerated blockwise sparse attention mechanism that supports both training from scratch and near-lossless conversion from pretrained GQA checkpoints.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We co-design efficient training and inference kernels that turn MSA’s theoretical compute savings into real wall-clock speedups at scale.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We perform extensive ablations scaling up to a 109B-parameter MoE model with native multimodal training, dissecting MSA’s behavior across scales and modalities.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2 </span>Preliminary</h2>

<section id="S2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.1 </span>Causal Attention and GQA</h3>

<div id="S2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We write <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> for the sequence length, <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\rm model}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\rm model}</annotation></semantics></math> for the hidden dimension, and <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> for the head dimension. For each query position <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and head <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>, causal Softmax Attention computes</p>
<table id="S2.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{o}}_{t}^{(h)}\;=\;\sum_{i\leq t}\alpha_{t,i}^{(h)}\,{\bm{v}}_{i}^{(h)},\qquad\alpha_{t,i}^{(h)}\;=\;\frac{\exp\!\big(\langle{\bm{q}}_{t}^{(h)},{\bm{k}}_{i}^{(h)}\rangle/\sqrt{d_{h}}\big)}{\sum_{j\leq t}\exp\!\big(\langle{\bm{q}}_{t}^{(h)},{\bm{k}}_{j}^{(h)}\rangle/\sqrt{d_{h}}\big)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒐</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.391em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒌</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒌</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{o}}_{t}^{(h)}\;=\;\sum_{i\leq t}\alpha_{t,i}^{(h)}\,{\bm{v}}_{i}^{(h)},\qquad\alpha_{t,i}^{(h)}\;=\;\frac{\exp\!\big(\langle{\bm{q}}_{t}^{(h)},{\bm{k}}_{i}^{(h)}\rangle/\sqrt{d_{h}}\big)}{\sum_{j\leq t}\exp\!\big(\langle{\bm{q}}_{t}^{(h)},{\bm{k}}_{j}^{(h)}\rangle/\sqrt{d_{h}}\big)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The cost of <a href="#S2.E1" title="In 2.1 Causal Attention and GQA ‣ 2 Preliminary ‣ MiniMax Sparse Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> is <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta(2H_{q}N^{2}d_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta(2H_{q}N^{2}d_{h})</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs, which grows quadratically with the sequence length <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>. Grouped-Query Attention <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ainslie et al., 2023</a>)</cite> uses <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> query heads and reduces the number of key-value heads to <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{kv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{kv}</annotation></semantics></math>, tying <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=H_{q}/H_{kv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=H_{q}/H_{kv}</annotation></semantics></math> adjacent query heads to a single shared key-value head. Thus, each key-value head defines one GQA group.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.2 </span>Sparse Attention as a Two-Stage Process</h3>

<div id="S2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A sparse attention layer factors causal attention into an indexer that selects which keys to attend to and a sparse attention computation over the selected keys. For each query position <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S2.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{I}}_{i}\;=\;\mathrm{Index}_{\phi}\!\big({\bm{q}}_{i},{\bm{K}}_{\leq i}\big),\qquad{\bm{o}}_{i}\;=\;\mathrm{Attn}\!\big({\bm{q}}_{i},{\bm{K}}[{\mathcal{I}}_{i}],{\bm{V}}[{\mathcal{I}}_{i}]\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Index</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑲</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒐</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.902em;" width="1.902em"><mi>Attn</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝑲</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{I}}_{i}\;=\;\mathrm{Index}_{\phi}\!\big({\bm{q}}_{i},{\bm{K}}_{\leq i}\big),\qquad{\bm{o}}_{i}\;=\;\mathrm{Attn}\!\big({\bm{q}}_{i},{\bm{K}}[{\mathcal{I}}_{i}],{\bm{V}}[{\mathcal{I}}_{i}]\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Index}_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Index</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Index}_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> is parameterized by <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> (empty for fixed-rule indexers; learned for trainable ones), <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{I}}_{i}\subseteq\{1,\dots,i\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{I}}_{i}\subseteq\{1,\dots,i\}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the selected index set, and <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Attn}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Attn</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Attn}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes standard scaled dot-product softmax attention restricted to this index set. We call the first stage the <em id="S2.SS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Index Branch</em> and the second the <em id="S2.SS2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Main Branch</em>. In multi-head attention, each query, specified by a position <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and a query head <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>, can select a different key/value index set, written as <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{I}}_{i}^{(h)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{I}}_{i}^{(h)}</annotation></semantics></math>; <a href="#S2.E2" title="In 2.2 Sparse Attention as a Two-Stage Process ‣ 2 Preliminary ‣ MiniMax Sparse Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> omits the head index only for notational simplicity.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.3 </span>GQA-Based Block Sparse Attention</h3>

<div id="S2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Per-head token-level selection offers the finest granularity, but such fine-grained computation is difficult to map efficiently to GPU matrix operations. For efficiency, sparse attention built on GQA can share the index result within each GQA group. Let <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> query heads served by the <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>-th key-value head. The group-shared index set can be written as</p>
<table id="S2.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{I}}_{i}^{(r)}={\mathcal{I}}_{i}^{(h)}={\mathcal{I}}_{i}^{(h^{\prime})},\qquad h,h^{\prime}\in\mathcal{H}_{r}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{I}}_{i}^{(r)}={\mathcal{I}}_{i}^{(h)}={\mathcal{I}}_{i}^{(h^{\prime})},\qquad h,h^{\prime}\in\mathcal{H}_{r}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Selecting key/value blocks rather than individual tokens reduces routing overhead and makes sparse attention more regular. For block size <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="S2.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathcal{B}}_{b}=\{(b{-}1)B_{k}+1,\dots,\min(bB_{k},N)\},\qquad b=1,\dots,B,\quad B=\lceil N/B_{k}\rceil." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{B}}_{b}=\{(b{-}1)B_{k}+1,\dots,\min(bB_{k},N)\},\qquad b=1,\dots,B,\quad B=\lceil N/B_{k}\rceil.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">For query position <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and GQA group <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, the set <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{I}}_{i}^{(r)}\subseteq\{1,\dots,B\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{I}}_{i}^{(r)}\subseteq\{1,\dots,B\}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the selected block index set.
The sparse attention output for any query head in group <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> is then computed over the causally visible tokens in the selected blocks, using the key-value head of the same group. <span id="S2.SS3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MSA</span> follows this GQA-based block sparse formulation, with the concrete indexer architecture and training objective described in the next section.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span><span id="S3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MSA</span></h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We introduce MiniMax Sparse Attention (<span id="S3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MSA</span>), a GQA-based sparse attention mechanism with two branches, as illustrated in Figure <a href="#S0.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ MiniMax Sparse Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. For each query token, a lightweight <em id="S3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Index Branch</em> selects a small set of key blocks from the causal context, and the <em id="S3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Main Branch</em> computes softmax attention over the tokens in those blocks. The Index Branch adds only two projection matrices to standard GQA, operates at block granularity, and makes selections independently for each GQA group. We describe the architecture in Section <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Architecture ‣ 3 MSA ‣ MiniMax Sparse Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> and the training procedure in Section <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Training ‣ 3 MSA ‣ MiniMax Sparse Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1 </span>Architecture</h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MSA</span> instantiates the two-stage sparse-attention formulation in Section <a href="#S2.SS2" title="2.2 Sparse Attention as a Two-Stage Process ‣ 2 Preliminary ‣ MiniMax Sparse Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a> at GQA-group and block granularity (Figure <a href="#S0.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ MiniMax Sparse Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>). For each query token, the Index Branch selects <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> key blocks of size <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> for each GQA group, and the Main Branch attends only to tokens in the selected blocks, whose budget is at most <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="kB_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">kB_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{X}}\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times d_{\rm model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{X}}\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times d_{\rm model}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the input hidden states. Following Section <a href="#S2.SS1" title="2.1 Causal Attention and GQA ‣ 2 Preliminary ‣ MiniMax Sparse Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>, we write <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{kv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{kv}</annotation></semantics></math> for the number of query heads and key-value heads, respectively, so each key-value head serves <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=H_{q}/H_{kv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=H_{q}/H_{kv}</annotation></semantics></math> query heads.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Index Branch.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Index Branch introduces one index query head for each GQA group and a single index key head shared across groups:</p>
<table id="S3.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{Q}}^{\rm idx}={\bm{X}}{\bm{W}}_{q}^{\rm idx}\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times H_{kv}\times d_{\rm idx}},\qquad{\bm{K}}^{\rm idx}={\bm{X}}{\bm{W}}_{k}^{\rm idx}\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times 1\times d_{\rm idx}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>idx</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>idx</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>idx</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>idx</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>idx</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>idx</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{Q}}^{\rm idx}={\bm{X}}{\bm{W}}_{q}^{\rm idx}\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times H_{kv}\times d_{\rm idx}},\qquad{\bm{K}}^{\rm idx}={\bm{X}}{\bm{W}}_{k}^{\rm idx}\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times 1\times d_{\rm idx}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For query token <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and group <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, the Index Branch first scores visible key tokens, then aggregates these scores to the block level. Using the block partition <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{B}}_{1},\dots,{\mathcal{B}}_{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{B}}_{1},\dots,{\mathcal{B}}_{B}</annotation></semantics></math> defined in Section <a href="#S2.SS3" title="2.3 GQA-Based Block Sparse Attention ‣ 2 Preliminary ‣ MiniMax Sparse Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>,</p>
<table id="S3.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{S}}^{\rm idx,(r)}_{i,j}\;=\;\frac{\bigl({\bm{Q}}^{\rm idx}\bigr)^{(r)}_{i}\,\bigl({\bm{K}}^{\rm idx}\bigr)_{j}^{\top}}{\sqrt{d_{\rm idx}}},\qquad M^{\rm idx,(r)}_{i,b}\;=\;\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}j\in{\mathcal{B}}_{b}\\
j\leq i\end{subarray}}{\bm{S}}^{\rm idx,(r)}_{i,j}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>idx</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>idx</mi></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>idx</mi></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>idx</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>idx</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑺</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>idx</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{S}}^{\rm idx,(r)}_{i,j}\;=\;\frac{\bigl({\bm{Q}}^{\rm idx}\bigr)^{(r)}_{i}\,\bigl({\bm{K}}^{\rm idx}\bigr)_{j}^{\top}}{\sqrt{d_{\rm idx}}},\qquad M^{\rm idx,(r)}_{i,b}\;=\;\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}j\in{\mathcal{B}}_{b}\\
j\leq i\end{subarray}}{\bm{S}}^{\rm idx,(r)}_{i,j}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> indexes the GQA group, <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\leq i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\leq i</annotation></semantics></math> enforces causality, and blocks with no visible token are assigned score <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. The Index Branch then selects the top-<math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> block indices:</p>
<table id="S3.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{I}}_{i}^{(r)}\;=\;\mathrm{TopK}_{b\in\{1,\dots,B\}}\!\bigl(M^{\rm idx,(r)}_{i,\cdot},\,k\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>TopK</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>idx</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{I}}_{i}^{(r)}\;=\;\mathrm{TopK}_{b\in\{1,\dots,B\}}\!\bigl(M^{\rm idx,(r)}_{i,\cdot},\,k\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TopK}(\cdot,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>TopK</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TopK}(\cdot,k)</annotation></semantics></math> returns the indices of the <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> largest blocks under <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\rm idx,(r)}_{i,\cdot}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>idx</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\rm idx,(r)}_{i,\cdot}</annotation></semantics></math>. We always include the local block containing position <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{I}}_{i}^{(r)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{I}}_{i}^{(r)}</annotation></semantics></math> is shared by all <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> query heads in group <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Main Branch.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given the block index set <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{I}}_{i}^{(r)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{I}}_{i}^{(r)}</annotation></semantics></math> selected by the Index Branch, the Main Branch attends only to the causally visible tokens in the selected blocks. For any query head <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in\mathcal{H}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in\mathcal{H}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, it applies standard scaled dot-product attention restricted to these tokens, using the key-value head associated with GQA group <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{O}}_{i}^{(h)}\;=\;\mathrm{softmax}\Biggl(\frac{{\bm{Q}}_{i}^{(h)}\,\bigl({\bm{K}}^{(r)}\!\bigl[{\mathcal{I}}_{i}^{(r)}\bigr]\bigr)^{\top}}{\sqrt{d_{h}}}\Biggr){\bm{V}}^{(r)}\!\bigl[{\mathcal{I}}_{i}^{(r)}\bigr]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑶</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑲</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{O}}_{i}^{(h)}\;=\;\mathrm{softmax}\Biggl(\frac{{\bm{Q}}_{i}^{(h)}\,\bigl({\bm{K}}^{(r)}\!\bigl[{\mathcal{I}}_{i}^{(r)}\bigr]\bigr)^{\top}}{\sqrt{d_{h}}}\Biggr){\bm{V}}^{(r)}\!\bigl[{\mathcal{I}}_{i}^{(r)}\bigr],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{Q}}_{i}^{(h)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{Q}}_{i}^{(h)}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the query vector at position <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and query head <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>, while <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{K}}^{(r)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝑲</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{K}}^{(r)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{V}}^{(r)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{V}}^{(r)}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the key and value matrices of the <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>-th GQA group.
The notation <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{K}}^{(r)}[{\mathcal{I}}_{i}^{(r)}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝑲</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{K}}^{(r)}[{\mathcal{I}}_{i}^{(r)}]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{V}}^{(r)}[{\mathcal{I}}_{i}^{(r)}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{V}}^{(r)}[{\mathcal{I}}_{i}^{(r)}]</annotation></semantics></math> denotes gathering the causally visible tokens from the selected blocks.
The block index set <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{I}}_{i}^{(r)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{I}}_{i}^{(r)}</annotation></semantics></math> is shared by all query heads in <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, while each head keeps its own query projection. Since the selected blocks contain at most <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="kB_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">kB_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> causally visible tokens, the per-query attention cost is reduced from <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(N)</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(kB_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(kB_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>, which is fixed as the sequence length increases.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Training</h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The top-<math id="S3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> selection in Equation <a href="#S3.E7" title="Equation 7 ‣ Index Branch. ‣ 3.1 Architecture ‣ 3 MSA ‣ MiniMax Sparse Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> is non-differentiable, so the language-modeling loss cannot train the index <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q/K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q/K</annotation></semantics></math> projections <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{W}}^{\rm idx}_{q},{\bm{W}}^{\rm idx}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>idx</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>idx</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{W}}^{\rm idx}_{q},{\bm{W}}^{\rm idx}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> directly. We therefore train the Index Branch with a KL alignment loss and use three mechanisms to stabilise sparse training: <span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Gradient Detach</span>, <span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Indexer Warmup</span>, and a forced <span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Local Block</span>. We describe each component below.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">KL Loss.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The KL loss gives the Index Branch a direct learning signal by matching its scores to the Main Branch on the selected tokens. Writing <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{I}}_{i,\mathrm{tok}}^{(r)}=(\bigcup_{b\in{\mathcal{I}}_{i}^{(r)}}{\mathcal{B}}_{b})\cap\{1,\dots,i\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>tok</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{I}}_{i,\mathrm{tok}}^{(r)}=(\bigcup_{b\in{\mathcal{I}}_{i}^{(r)}}{\mathcal{B}}_{b})\cap\{1,\dots,i\}</annotation></semantics></math> for the causally visible tokens induced by the selected block indices, for each query position <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and GQA group <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the Index Branch distribution <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\rm idx}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>idx</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\rm idx}</annotation></semantics></math> and the Main Branch teacher <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> over this token index set:</p>
<table id="S3.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{{\rm idx},(r)}_{i,j}=\frac{\exp(S^{{\rm idx},(r)}_{i,j})}{\sum_{u\in{\mathcal{I}}_{i,\mathrm{tok}}^{(r)}}\exp(S^{{\rm idx},(r)}_{i,u})},\qquad P^{(r)}_{i,j}=\frac{1}{G}\sum_{\ell\in\mathcal{H}_{r}}\frac{\exp(S^{(\ell)}_{i,j})}{\sum_{u\in{\mathcal{I}}_{i,\mathrm{tok}}^{(r)}}\exp(S^{(\ell)}_{i,u})},\qquad j\in{\mathcal{I}}_{i,\mathrm{tok}}^{(r)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>idx</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>idx</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>tok</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>idx</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>G</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>tok</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>tok</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{{\rm idx},(r)}_{i,j}=\frac{\exp(S^{{\rm idx},(r)}_{i,j})}{\sum_{u\in{\mathcal{I}}_{i,\mathrm{tok}}^{(r)}}\exp(S^{{\rm idx},(r)}_{i,u})},\qquad P^{(r)}_{i,j}=\frac{1}{G}\sum_{\ell\in\mathcal{H}_{r}}\frac{\exp(S^{(\ell)}_{i,j})}{\sum_{u\in{\mathcal{I}}_{i,\mathrm{tok}}^{(r)}}\exp(S^{(\ell)}_{i,u})},\qquad j\in{\mathcal{I}}_{i,\mathrm{tok}}^{(r)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{{\rm idx},(r)}_{i,j}=({\bm{Q}}^{\rm idx})^{(r)}_{i}({\bm{K}}^{\rm idx})_{j}^{\top}/\sqrt{d_{\rm idx}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>idx</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>idx</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>idx</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>idx</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{{\rm idx},(r)}_{i,j}=({\bm{Q}}^{\rm idx})^{(r)}_{i}({\bm{K}}^{\rm idx})_{j}^{\top}/\sqrt{d_{\rm idx}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the token-level index score, and <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{(\ell)}_{i,j}={\bm{Q}}^{(\ell)}_{i}({\bm{K}}^{(r)}_{j})^{\top}/\sqrt{d_{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{(\ell)}_{i,j}={\bm{Q}}^{(\ell)}_{i}({\bm{K}}^{(r)}_{j})^{\top}/\sqrt{d_{h}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the Main Branch score for query head <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in\mathcal{H}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in\mathcal{H}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>. The teacher <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> averages the per-head Main Branch distributions at the probability level. The indexer is then trained to match <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>, averaged over all query positions and GQA groups:</p>
<table id="S3.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\rm KL}=\frac{1}{NH_{kv}}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{r=1}^{H_{kv}}D_{\mathrm{KL}}\bigl(\mathrm{stopgrad}(P^{(r)}_{i,\cdot})\,\|\,P^{{\rm idx},(r)}_{i,\cdot}\bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub></munderover><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>stopgrad</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>idx</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\rm KL}=\frac{1}{NH_{kv}}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{r=1}^{H_{kv}}D_{\mathrm{KL}}\bigl(\mathrm{stopgrad}(P^{(r)}_{i,\cdot})\,\|\,P^{{\rm idx},(r)}_{i,\cdot}\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> is the sequence length, and the teacher distribution <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{(r)}_{i,\cdot}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{(r)}_{i,\cdot}</annotation></semantics></math> is detached from gradient computation. This auxiliary loss aligns the index distribution with the Main Branch attention pattern, making the subsequent block selection semantically meaningful.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Gradient Detach.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To isolate the auxiliary objective from the backbone, we apply stop-gradient to the Index Branch input:</p>
<table id="S3.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{Q}}^{\rm idx}\;=\;\mathrm{stopgrad}({\bm{X}}){\bm{W}}^{\rm idx}_{q},\qquad{\bm{K}}^{\rm idx}\;=\;\mathrm{stopgrad}({\bm{X}}){\bm{W}}^{\rm idx}_{k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>idx</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>stopgrad</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>idx</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>idx</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>stopgrad</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>idx</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{Q}}^{\rm idx}\;=\;\mathrm{stopgrad}({\bm{X}}){\bm{W}}^{\rm idx}_{q},\qquad{\bm{K}}^{\rm idx}\;=\;\mathrm{stopgrad}({\bm{X}}){\bm{W}}^{\rm idx}_{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The teacher <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> in Equation <a href="#S3.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ KL Loss. ‣ 3.2 Training ‣ 3 MSA ‣ MiniMax Sparse Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> is detached, so <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\rm KL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\rm KL}</annotation></semantics></math> leaves the Main Branch projections untouched; Equation <a href="#S3.E11" title="Equation 11 ‣ Gradient Detach. ‣ 3.2 Training ‣ 3 MSA ‣ MiniMax Sparse Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> further prevents it from reaching the backbone through <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑿</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Under this rule, <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\rm KL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\rm KL}</annotation></semantics></math> updates only <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{W}}^{\rm idx}_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>idx</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{W}}^{\rm idx}_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{W}}^{\rm idx}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>idx</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{W}}^{\rm idx}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, making the KL a clean alignment signal for the indexer.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Indexer Warmup.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use a two-stage training schedule to initialise the Index Branch and avoid early random selections. During the first few iterations, the model runs full attention in both branches and trains the newly added index projections with <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\rm KL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\rm KL}</annotation></semantics></math>. After warmup, the model switches to sparse attention, and <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\rm KL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\rm KL}</annotation></semantics></math> is computed over the top-<math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> selected positions. The same schedule is used when sparsifying a pretrained full-attention checkpoint, which helps align the newly added index projections before they control Main Branch routing.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Local Block.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each query position <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and GQA group <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, the local block containing <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is always selected as part of <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{I}}_{i}^{(r)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{I}}_{i}^{(r)}</annotation></semantics></math> during both training and inference. This fixed allocation reserves one block slot and leaves the remaining slots to be chosen by the Index Branch, preventing degenerate selections that omit the query’s immediate neighbourhood.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The complete layer-level training procedure is summarised in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Local Block. ‣ 3.2 Training ‣ 3 MSA ‣ MiniMax Sparse Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> One <span id="alg1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MSA</span> layer: training forward and the auxiliary KL loss. The layer returns its output and per-layer <math id="alg1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\rm KL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\rm KL}</annotation></semantics></math>; the model loss <math id="alg1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}=\mathcal{L}_{\rm LM}+\lambda\sum_{\rm layers}\mathcal{L}_{\rm KL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>LM</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>layers</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}=\mathcal{L}_{\rm LM}+\lambda\sum_{\rm layers}\mathcal{L}_{\rm KL}</annotation></semantics></math> is assembled by the training loop.</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l0.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">0:</span></span>
                
                
               hidden states <math id="alg1.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{X}}\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times d_{\rm model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{X}}\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times d_{\rm model}}</annotation></semantics></math>; block size <math id="alg1.l0.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>,
number of selected blocks <math id="alg1.l0.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
                
                
               <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{Q}},{\bm{K}},{\bm{V}}\leftarrow{\bm{X}}{\bm{W}}_{q},\,{\bm{X}}{\bm{W}}_{k},\,{\bm{X}}{\bm{W}}_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑸</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑲</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝑽</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{Q}},{\bm{K}},{\bm{V}}\leftarrow{\bm{X}}{\bm{W}}_{q},\,{\bm{X}}{\bm{W}}_{k},\,{\bm{X}}{\bm{W}}_{v}</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="alg1.l1.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><span id="alg1.l1.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">// <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(N,H_{q},d_{h}),(N,H_{kv},d_{h}),(N,H_{kv},d_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">N</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">H</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">q</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">d</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">h</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">,</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">N</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">H</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">v</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">d</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">h</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">,</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">N</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">H</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">v</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">d</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">h</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(N,H_{q},d_{h}),(N,H_{kv},d_{h}),(N,H_{kv},d_{h})</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
                
                
               <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{Q}}^{\rm idx},{\bm{K}}^{\rm idx}\leftarrow\mathrm{stopgrad}({\bm{X}}){\bm{W}}^{\rm idx}_{q},\,\mathrm{stopgrad}({\bm{X}}){\bm{W}}^{\rm idx}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>idx</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>idx</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>stopgrad</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>idx</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>stopgrad</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>idx</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{Q}}^{\rm idx},{\bm{K}}^{\rm idx}\leftarrow\mathrm{stopgrad}({\bm{X}}){\bm{W}}^{\rm idx}_{q},\,\mathrm{stopgrad}({\bm{X}}){\bm{W}}^{\rm idx}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="alg1.l2.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><span id="alg1.l2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">// <math id="alg1.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(N,H_{kv},d_{\rm idx}),(N,1,d_{\rm idx})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">N</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">H</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">v</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">d</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">idx</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">,</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">N</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">d</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">idx</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(N,H_{kv},d_{\rm idx}),(N,1,d_{\rm idx})</annotation></semantics></math>; detached</span>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
                
                
               <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\rm idx}\leftarrow\mathrm{BlockMaxPool}({\bm{Q}}^{\rm idx},{\bm{K}}^{\rm idx},B_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>idx</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>BlockMaxPool</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>idx</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>idx</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\rm idx}\leftarrow\mathrm{BlockMaxPool}({\bm{Q}}^{\rm idx},{\bm{K}}^{\rm idx},B_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><span id="alg1.l3.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">// <math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(N,H_{kv},B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">N</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">H</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">v</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">B</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(N,H_{kv},B)</annotation></semantics></math>; per-group, causal</span>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
                
                
               <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{I}}\leftarrow\mathrm{TopK}(M^{\rm idx},\,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>TopK</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>idx</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{I}}\leftarrow\mathrm{TopK}(M^{\rm idx},\,k)</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="alg1.l4.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><span id="alg1.l4.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">// selected block indices; local block included</span>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
                
                
               <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{O}}\leftarrow\mathrm{TopKAttn}({\bm{Q}},{\bm{K}},{\bm{V}},{\mathcal{I}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑶</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>TopKAttn</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑸</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑲</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{O}}\leftarrow\mathrm{TopKAttn}({\bm{Q}},{\bm{K}},{\bm{V}},{\mathcal{I}})</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="alg1.l5.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><span id="alg1.l5.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">// <math id="alg1.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(N,H_{q},d_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">N</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">H</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">q</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">d</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">h</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(N,H_{q},d_{h})</annotation></semantics></math>; attends to selected blocks</span>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
                
                
               <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{output}\leftarrow{\bm{O}}{\bm{W}}_{o}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>output</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>𝑶</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{output}\leftarrow{\bm{O}}{\bm{W}}_{o}</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="alg1.l6.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><span id="alg1.l6.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">// <math id="alg1.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(N,d_{\rm model})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">N</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">d</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080">model</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" mathcolor="#808080" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(N,d_{\rm model})</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
                
                
               <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\rm KL}\leftarrow\mathrm{KLdiv}({\bm{Q}}^{\rm idx},{\bm{K}}^{\rm idx},\,\mathrm{stopgrad}({\bm{Q}}),\mathrm{stopgrad}({\bm{K}}),\,{\mathcal{I}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>KLdiv</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑸</mi><mi>idx</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>idx</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>stopgrad</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑸</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>stopgrad</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\rm KL}\leftarrow\mathrm{KLdiv}({\bm{Q}}^{\rm idx},{\bm{K}}^{\rm idx},\,\mathrm{stopgrad}({\bm{Q}}),\mathrm{stopgrad}({\bm{K}}),\,{\mathcal{I}})</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="alg1.l7.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><span id="alg1.l7.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">// over tokens induced by <math id="alg1.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{I}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#808080">ℐ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{I}}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
                
                
               <span id="alg1.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{output},\ \mathcal{L}_{\rm KL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>output</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{output},\ \mathcal{L}_{\rm KL}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3 </span>Computational Complexity</h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Under the same <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{q}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{kv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{kv}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, and sequence length <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, the causal attention FLOPs of GQA and <span id="S3.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MSA</span> are</p>
<table id="S3.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\rm GQA}(N)=2H_{q}d_{h}N^{2},\qquad F_{\textsc{MSA}{}}(N)=\underbrace{H_{kv}d_{\rm idx}N^{2}}_{\text{Index Branch}}+\underbrace{4H_{q}d_{h}NkB_{k}}_{\text{Main Branch}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>GQA</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">MSA</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>idx</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Index Branch</mtext></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Main Branch</mtext></munder></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\rm GQA}(N)=2H_{q}d_{h}N^{2},\qquad F_{\textsc{MSA}{}}(N)=\underbrace{H_{kv}d_{\rm idx}N^{2}}_{\text{Index Branch}}+\underbrace{4H_{q}d_{h}NkB_{k}}_{\text{Main Branch}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">GQA scales its main attention path with the full context length, whereas <span id="S3.SS3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MSA</span> uses a fixed selection budget <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="kB_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">kB_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> plus a lightweight index computation; the FLOPs gap therefore grows with <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="kB_{k}\ll N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≪</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">kB_{k}\ll N</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{kv}d_{\rm idx}\ll H_{q}d_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>idx</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≪</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{kv}d_{\rm idx}\ll H_{q}d_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Kernel Design</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section describes the GPU kernels used in our sparse prefill implementation, including the index TopK kernel, the KV-outer sparse attention forward, and the sparse KL loss backward.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Index &amp; TopK</h3>

<section id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Exp-free selection.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To efficiently select the top-<math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> KV blocks, the index module ranks the index scores <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> directly. Since softmax is order-preserving, the relative ordering of scores is preserved (<math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}\leq s_{j}\iff\mathrm{softmax}(s)_{i}\leq\mathrm{softmax}(s)_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}\leq s_{j}\iff\mathrm{softmax}(s)_{i}\leq\mathrm{softmax}(s)_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>), leaving the top-<math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> indices unchanged. The forward pass, therefore, bypasses the max/exp/sum steps of softmax and passes raw scores directly to selection.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Per-thread register top-<math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The block size <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and selection size <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> are co-designed with the top-<math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> kernel: a large <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> increases attention arithmetic intensity (Section <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Sparse Attention ‣ 4 Kernel Design ‣ MiniMax Sparse Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>), and a small <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> at this <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> keeps both the per-row candidate block count <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> below the sweet spot of general-purpose top-<math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> kernels, which amortize multi-pass bucketing over large <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> (radix selection) or scale as <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(B\log^{2}B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(B\log^{2}B)</annotation></semantics></math> (bitonic sort). We adopt <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{k}=128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{k}=128</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=16</annotation></semantics></math>. Each of the warp’s 32 lanes streams a 1/32 stride of the input row and maintains a <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-element min-heap in shared memory. The heap root is cached in a register, and insertions are performed with deferred writes. Finally, a <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-round shuffle merge combines the 32 local TopK results. The shared-memory layout maps each lane to a fixed bank, avoiding conflicts.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Benchmark.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We compare against <span id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">torch.topk</span> and the TileLang <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib71" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2025</a>)</cite> radix-select top-<math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> on an H800 GPU with <span id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">fp32</span> inputs and unsorted outputs; latencies are the median of <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>50</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50</annotation></semantics></math> post-warmup iterations. Table <a href="#S4.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ Benchmark. ‣ 4.1 Index &amp; TopK ‣ 4 Kernel Design ‣ MiniMax Sparse Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> shows that our specialized kernel is fastest in all tested settings, with the largest gains at the deployed setting <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=16</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T1" class="ltx_table">
<table id="S4.T1.3" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S4.T1.3.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T1.3.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Seq. Len. <math id="S4.T1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="S4.T1.3.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Blocks <math id="S4.T1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math></th>
